es people another route into books. A broad reading community can include that route without demanding one sensory method.","counters":[]},{"id":"for_oral_tradition","side":"for","answer":"Oral tradition","aliases":["oral storytelling","storytelling tradition","spoken tradition","spoken literature","oral literature","oral stories","spoken stories","oral narrative","storytellers","storytelling","spoken word tradition","stories aloud","oral culture","narrative tradition","listening tradition","folktales","stories before print","stories through voices","spoken literary tradition","oral literary tradition","voice based storytelling","stories by voice","stories passed orally","oral transmission","oral story tradition","oral story culture","listening to literature","hearing literature","spoken narrative tradition","oral literary culture","storytelling culture","stories without print"],"tier":"clever","points":50,"reveal":"Stories and literary traditions travel through voices as well as pages. Silent print is not the only way to encounter a work.","counters":[]},{"id":"for_brain_processing","side":"for","answer":"Semantic processing","aliases":["brain processing","semantic maps","semantic map","brain maps","brain scan","brain scans","brain study","meaning processing","semantic networks","language networks","similar semantic processing","same meaning networks","neural semantics","semantic information","brain language processing","similar meaning maps","similar brain meaning maps","similar semantic maps","similar brain maps","shared semantic maps","shared meaning processing","shared semantic processing","semantic processing similarity","meaning network similarity","neural meaning maps","neuroscience study","fmri study","language meaning maps","cortical meaning maps","shared meaning representation","meaning representation","similar semantic networks"],"tier":"deep-cut","points":75,"reveal":"A study found similar cortical meaning maps for listening and reading stories. Shared 