er reads and the listener listens; a shared reading event still contains different participant roles."}]},{"id":"against_visual_form","side":"against","answer":"Visual composition","aliases":["page layout","typography","line breaks","visual poetry","concrete poetry","diagrams","illustrations","tables","visual form","printed form","italics","font changes","footnote layout","text arrangement","visual relationships","typographic meaning","visual text arrangement","text on page","page design","page structure","layout carries meaning","typography carries meaning","line breaks matter","visual formatting","printed layout","textual layout","diagram relationships","visual diagrams","formatting on page","spacing on page","poem shape","poetry line breaks"],"tier":"deep-cut","points":75,"reveal":"Line breaks, typography, diagrams, and page relationships can be part of a work. Sound may translate those rather than present the same form.","counters":[{"targetId":"for_same_words","reveal":"Keeping the words need not keep line breaks, diagrams, or typographic relationships."}]},{"id":"against_spatial_anchors","side":"against","answer":"Page landmarks","aliases":["spatial memory","page memory","spatial anchors","where on page","paragraph position","page position","margin notes","visual landmarks","spatial layout","remember the page","location on page","page geography","physical location","page orientation","spatial reading landmarks","visual page memory","location in book","location in text","paragraph location","position of paragraph","top of page","bottom of page","margin location","remember paragraph location","spatial book memory","visual orientation","where text appears","where paragraph appears","page based landmarks","spatial navigation cues"],"tier":"clever","points":50,"reveal":"A page provides spatial landmarks: a paragraph near the top or a note in the margin. Audio timestamps organize memory differently.","counters":[]},{"id":"against_quote_precision","side":"against","a